coole is built from a release archive created by
packaging/release-source.sh with "meson dist".  The archive carries the
version in .tarball-version: a build outside Git would otherwise report it
as "unknown".

This directory carries no version.  debian/changelog is generated by
packaging/prepare.sh from the annotated coole-* tags, and is listed in
.gitignore.  Its entries are the tag messages and its dates are the tag dates,
so the same tag always yields the same source package.

To build the source package for a version, take the release archive and copy
this directory into it.  Building from the Git checkout instead would add the
whole of packaging/ as a patch, and record the absence of .tarball-version.  For a
version X.Y.Z tagged coole-X.Y.Z:

  packaging/release-source.sh X.Y.Z coole-X.Y.Z
  packaging/prepare.sh X.Y.Z dist/coole-X.Y.Z.tar.gz
  tar -xf dist/coole-X.Y.Z.tar.gz -C /tmp
  cp dist/coole-X.Y.Z.tar.gz /tmp/coole_X.Y.Z.orig.tar.gz
  cp -r debian /tmp/coole-X.Y.Z/
  cd /tmp/coole-X.Y.Z && dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

A version without a tag of its own is a test build: prepare.sh marks its entry
UNRELEASED, and dput refuses such a package.  For a PPA, name the target series
and add a series suffix to the version:

  DEB_DISTRIBUTION=noble DEB_VERSION_SUFFIX='~ubuntu24.04.1' \
      packaging/prepare.sh X.Y.Z dist/coole-X.Y.Z.tar.gz

Files taken from gnulib
-----------------------

lib/strutil/filevercmp.c and lib/strutil/strverscmp.c come from gnulib, which is a source library: it is copied
into a tree and built with it, and there is no shared library to link against
instead. The Debian gnulib package is Architecture: all and carries sources
only. The files here were taken by hand, not with gnulib-tool, which is why the
tree has no bootstrap.conf and no gnulib-cache.m4, and why their vintage
differs from file to file; the years are in each header. They are adapted to
this tree: strverscmp.c includes config.h and lib/strutil.h and carries a
second notice of its own. Every one of them is declared in debian/copyright
with the license of its own, LGPL-2.1+ or LGPL-3+, not the GPL-3+ of the rest.

Generated files in the archive
------------------------------

The release archive is made by "meson dist" from the Git tree and carries no
generated build files; the only file added to it is .tarball-version.
